{"type":"message","id":"072c631a","parentId":"8843806c","timestamp":"2026-03-26T11:05:34.127Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I can see the issue clearly:\n\n1. The most recent run (just now) timed out after **600,014 ms** (~10 minutes). The timeout is set to 10 minutes (600s).\n2. The previous run succeeded in ~120 seconds (2 minutes) with status \"ok\".\n\nSo the job CAN succeed (it did in 2 minutes previously), but sometimes it times out at 10 minutes. This suggests the issue might be:\n1. Network variability causing the gh api commands to hang occasionally\n2. GitHub API rate limiting\n3. The job sometimes taking longer than 10 minutes\n\nThe timeout is 10 minutes (600,000 ms) and the last run hit exactly that limit. \n\nThe previous successful run only took 2 minutes, so the real problem is that the job occasionally hangs—possibly when hitting GitHub's rate limits or facing network issues. I should suggest increasing the cron timeout to something more generous like 15-20 minutes, and potentially add a shorter built-in timeout for the individual gh api calls with retry logic. The fact that it ran successfully before means the job itself works; it just needs more headroom on the timeout and better error handling for when GitHub becomes unresponsive.","thinkingSignature":"bcd34023772b00dd90a093d5b90e3d6d82792223269bb3dbbc4ba378f94d6e4d"},{"type":"text","text":"找到原因了：\n\n**上次成功**：耗时 ~120秒，正常完成\n**这次失败**：耗时刚好 600,014 ms（10分钟），触达 **cron 执行 timeout 上限**\n\n说明任务本身没问题，但偶尔会跑得久（GitHub API 响应慢或 rate limit）。10分钟 timeout 太紧。\n\n**解决方案**：把 timeout 调大。跑个诊断先确认 gh api 响应是否正常：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_o1vr9j1kd231_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"timeout 30 gh api repos/openclaw/openclaw/issues/54952/comments --jq 'length' 2>&1; echo \"exit: $?\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":15427,"output":394,"cacheRead":22191,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":38012,"c