{"type":"message","id":"be441e51","parentId":"1812f296","timestamp":"2026-03-26T11:18:58.218Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Ah, there's the constraint. Main session jobs can only use `--system-event`, not `--message` (agentTurn). So I can't change this to an agentTurn job.\n\nThe problem is that for systemEvent crons targeting the main session, the timeout can't be set via CLI. The gateway seems to apply a hard timeout.\n\nLet me think about this differently. The issue is:\n1. The feedback check cron runs on `main` session with `systemEvent`\n2. `main` session is a persistent session\n3. The gateway might be applying a 600s (10min) timeout to systemEvent cron jobs for main session\n\nOptions:\n1. Run the feedback check as an isolated session instead - but this would change the behavior\n\n\n2. Add failure alerting so we get notified when it fails instead of having it silently timeout\n3. Check if there's a gateway config that controls systemEvent timeout for main sessions\n\nActually, the morning briefing error had a slightly different message format, which suggests the underlying issue might be the same - the systemEvent payload against the main session just hits a gateway-level timeout that I can't override. The morning briefing is an agentTurn, but the feedback check is a systemEvent, and maybe that distinction matters for how the timeout is enforced.\n\nI could try configuring the gateway directly, but I'm realizing the feedback check cron is already set to 30 minutes and has been running successfully with a 120-second duration before - the 600-second timeout was only hit once. Maybe the real issue is just that GitHub API calls are occasionally slow, and this will resolve on its own.\n\nLooking at the three failing jobs, the OpenClaw feedback check uses systemEvent while the morning briefing and evening workspace use agentTurn - both types are hitting timeouts, which suggests the problem isn't payload-specific but rather how the gateway handles timeouts for these session types. The morning briefing has failure alerts configured but still timed out, so increasing the timeout duration might be the better approach rather than relying on alerting alone.\n\nWait, I'm realizing the core issue: systemEvent payloads against the main session appear to have a hard 600-second timeout that can't be overridden via CLI, and the feedback check cron is doing multiple GitHub API calls that are hanging. The real solution here is to make the task more resilient - I could rewrite the feedback check script to use shorter individual command timeouts with `timeout` wrappers, and if an API call fails, just skip it rather than hanging indefinitely.","thinkingSignature":"ddcce609715539babe13a420c5c0c8510a67fa9895e0f01b200e0553925eedde"},{"type":"text","text":"主 session 的 systemEvent cron 有硬性 timeout 上限，无法通过 CLI 改。有两个解法：\n\n1. **把反馈检查改成 isolated session**（避免占用主 session）\n2. **给 gh api 加上单次 timeout 保护**，防止单次调用卡死导致整任务超时\n\n方案 2 更干净，不改变 session 归属。让我重写这个任务的消息，加上 `timeout` 保护：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_zzr7bsbzvl45_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"openclaw cron add \\\n  --name \"OpenClaw 反馈检查\" \\\n  --every 30m \\\n  --session main \\\n  --system-event \"OpenClaw贡献项目每30分钟定时检查。步骤：1) 读取 /root/.openclaw/workspace/memory/OPENCLAW-PROJECT.md；2) 用 gh api 检查 #54952 #54964 #55008 #55013 是否有新反馈（每次 gh api 加 timeout 15秒防卡死：timeout 15 gh api ...）；3) 如有反馈则更新 OPENCLAW-PROJECT.md 并输出简短进展；4) 如无反馈直接回复 NO_REPLY；5) 全程禁止 git commit。\" \\\n  2>&1 | tail -3"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":24379,"output":772,"cacheRead":22191,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":47342,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774523916041}}
