{"type":"message","id":"06fcea63","parentId":"26b86b40","timestamp":"2026-03-26T11:55:29.848Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The cron actually ran successfully! It checked all the issues, found that ling had already fixed the PRs, noted that the Greptile review comments are stale (since ling already fixed the issues), and concluded that there's no new feedback from maintainers.\n\nBut then why does the cron run say \"error: AxiosError: Request failed with status code 400\"?\n\nWait - the cron run shows the session completed with a \"stop\" (not error). But the cron run history says error. Let me look at this more carefully.\n\nActually, looking at the output again: the session ended with `\"stopReason\":\"stop\"` meaning the agent completed its work normally. But the cron run record says error with \"AxiosError: Request failed with status code 400\".\n\n\nThe 400 error might be coming from the cron scheduler's own attempt to deliver the result, not from the agent itself. If the delivery was attempted via webhook and failed with a 400, that would explain why the cron run shows an error even though the agent completed successfully. So the cron system tried to deliver the result to the Feishu channel but got a 400 error back from the webhook - that would explain the AxiosError in the cron run record, even though the agent itself ran fine. The gateway might be using a different API to send messages to Feishu than what I'm testing locally, which could explain why the webhook delivery is failing. The model was actually working fine - it completed successfully and replied with NO_REPLY. The cron run shows an error, but the delivery status of \"not-requested\" suggests the issue is with how the result was being delivered back to the user, not with the actual task execution. The \"AxiosError: Request failed with status code 400\" likely came from the delivery mechanism trying to announce to the Feishu chat, not from the gh api calls themselves. So the cron error the user is seeing is probably a false alarm - the underlying task ran fine, but something broke in the reporting back to them. The cron payload has delivery mode \"none\" and there's no announce flag, so it shouldn't be trying to deliver anywhere. The session target is \"isolated\" which means it's running in its own context, not the main session - that's why it's not reporting back here.\n\nBut looking at the actual cron run history, it's showing an error with \"AxiosError: Request failed with status code 400\" and a duration of 75 seconds, which suggests the cron itself is failing, not just the delivery. The session completed with \"stop\" which indicates normal completion, but the error might be happening during the delivery phase after the session finishes.\n\nThe root cause is probably the cron re-delivery mechanism trying to announce to Feishu but getting a 400 error from the webhook. Since the original payload doesn't have `--announce`, I need to figure out how to properly configure this. The delivery mode is \"none\" in the cron job config, so something else must be triggering the webhook call.\n\nLet me just verify the cron actually ran successfully by checking the feedback check file.","thinkingSignature":"1e3c1c5434fe65cd6315fc089ff4fbd35f0b0e1ba603fdcbef1d33a0d051baa6"},{"type":"text","text":"Cron 本身执行成功了（session transcript 全程正常），但 cron **投递回报**失败。让我看具体哪步报错：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_iqx8velbtmt5_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cat /root/.openclaw/workspace/memory/openclaw-feedback-check.txt 2>/dev/null | tail -20"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":30247,"output":709,"cacheRead":22191,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":53147,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774526110155}}
{"type":"message","id":"536e9c53","parentId":"06fcea63","timestamp":"2026-03-26T11:55:29.888Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_iqx8velbtmt5_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"--- 2026-03-26 18:17 (UTC) / 2026-03-27 02:17 (UTC+8) ---\n\n#54952 (issue): 无新动态。0 条评论。\n\n#54964 (issue): 无新动态。0 条评论。\n\n#55008 (PR): 有新动态。Greptile 自动化 review 1 条：\n  - 指出 PR 移除了 feishu 插件 manifest 中的 \"skills\": [\"./skills\"] 条目，但 ./skills 目录仍存在且包含4个 skill 定义（feishu-doc/drive/perm/wiki），会导致这些 skills 无法注册，属意外删除。建议 revert 两处文件。\n\n#55013 (PR): 有新动态。共3条评论：\n  - Greptile x2：指出 groupPolicy 是访问控制（决定消息是否被接受），而非 agent 选择，agent 由 defaultAccount 决定。两处文档措辞有误并给出修正建议。\n  - ChatGPT-Codex x1：同样指出 groupPolicy fallback 行为描述错误，agent 路由不使用 groupPolicy 做决策。"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":19,"aggregated":"--- 2026-03-26 18:17 (UTC) / 2026-03-27 02:17 (UTC+8) ---\n\n#54952 (issue): 无新动态。0 条评论。\n\n#54964 (issue): 无新动态。0 条评论。\n\n#55008 (PR): 有新动态。Greptile 自动化 review 1 条：\n  - 指出 PR 移除了 feishu 插件 manifest 中的 \"skills\": [\"./skills\"] 条目，但 ./skills 目录仍存在且包含4个 skill 定义（feishu-doc/drive/perm/wiki），会导致这些 skills 无法注册，属意外删除。建议 revert 两处文件。\n\n#55013 (PR): 有新动态。共3条评论：\n  - Greptile x2：指出 groupPolicy 是访问控制（决定消息是否被接受），而非 agent 选择，agent 由 defaultAccount 决定。两处文档措辞有误并给出修正建议。\n  - ChatGPT-Codex x1：同样指出 groupPolicy fallback 行为描述错误，agent 路由不使用 groupPolicy 做决策。","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774526129868}}
{"type":"message","id":"63224e74","parentId":"536e9c53","timestamp":"2026-03-26T11:55:58.090Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The feedback check file is from 18:17. But the cron ran again at 19:49 and also failed. Let me check if there's another entry in the file from 19:49.\n\nActually, looking at the timeline:\n- 18:17: Last successful feedback check\n- 19:00: ling fixed the PRs  \n- 19:49: Cron ran but got \"error\" - delivery 400 error\n\nSo the cron ran and got results (found the stale Greptile comments), but then failed when trying to report back to the Feishu channel.\n\nThe \"error\" status in cron is because the **delivery** of the result to the Feishu chat failed (400 from Feishu API), not because the task itself failed.\n \nNow I'm seeing that the cron delivery is returning \"not-requested\" which suggests the cron system tried to send a notification to Feishu but got a 400 error back - the main session's announcement webhook might have different credentials or permissions than what the cron system is using.\n\nThe core issue is that the isolated cron session with `delivery: mode: \"none\"` shouldn't be attempting any delivery at all, yet something is triggering a webhook call that fails. This could mean the cron was already broken before my changes, or the 19:49 run had a different configuration that's causing the webhook attempt.\n\nLooking at the timing from the transcript, the agent finished normally at 19:50:39 and said \"Now let me reply with the summary as required\" - which should have returned NO_REPLY since there was no new feedback. But the cron still shows an error afterward, suggesting something went wrong in the reporting phase itself rather than during execution. The 400 error might actually be a red herring—the cron completed successfully but the delivery webhook to Feishu failed, which is why it's showing as errored. This points to a gateway configuration issue rather than something I can fix in the cron job itself.\n\nLooking at the cron list output, there are four cron jobs total with three in error state, but they all ran fine previously. This started happening after the session was switched to isolated mode at 19:49. I'm wondering if there's a mismatch between how the main session and isolated sessions handle webhook delivery, or if the cron job's payload structure changed in a way that's causing the gateway to attempt delivery when it shouldn't. main` session is different from `isolated` session in terms of what the cron runner considers \"delivery\". When `sessionTarget=main` was set before, the cron knew to deliver to the main session. When it's `isolated`, maybe the cron system tries to announce to feishu as a fallback.\n\nActually, I just realized: the `OpenClaw 反馈检查` cron was recreated as `isolated` session at around 19:20. The cron run at 19:49 was with the new `isolated` session config. Before my changes, it was a `main` session and had the same timeout issue.\n\nWait - let me re-read the original cron run history. Before my changes, the feedback check ran twice: once at 18:07 (ok, 120s) and once at 18:32 (error, 600s timeout).\n\nSo the error count is 2 for the old `main` session and 1 for the new `isolated` session. The delivery 400 error is a separate problem from the timeout issue. The user asked \"怎么没有触发\" meaning they didn't see the notification appear in the Feishu group - that's because the delivery failed with a 400 error.\n\nSo there are two distinct problems: the original timeout error when it was a `main` session (now fixed with longer timeout and isolated session), and now a delivery 400 error with the `isolated` session that I need to investigate separately.","thinkingSignature":"af8588d8fb15b5036fbdb9460134ace6f7f457e5c295fd1a0726356fbf5d678a"},{"type":"text","text":"\n[[reply_to_current]]\n\n找到根因了！Cron **任务本身执行正常**（session 全程正常跑完，Gh api 全部成功），但 **cron 回报投递到飞书失败**（400 错误）。\n\n任务输出显示没有新的 maintainer 反馈（Greptile review 是旧的，ling 已经修复了），所以最后回复了 NO_REPLY。但 cron 系统试图向飞书发回报时，收到 400 错误，导致整个 cron 标记为 error。\n\n**这个 400 是 cron 投递机制的问题，不是任务本身的问题。**\n\n让我确认一下当前 cron 的投递配置：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_a86ulo22xx0t_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"openclaw cron list --json 2>&1 | python3 -c \"\nimport json,sys\ndata=json.load(sys.stdin)\ncron = next(j for j in data['jobs'] if j['id']=='5bc9519b-f4e2-4719-ba7b-67f8773049bd')\nprint('delivery mode:', cron.get('delivery',{}).get('mode'))\nprint('announce:', cron.get('payload',{}).get('announce'))\nprint('sessionTarget:', cron.get('sessionTarget'))\nprint('wakeMode:', cron.get('wakeMode'))\n\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":31201,"output":1066,"cacheRead":22191,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":54458,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774526129887}}
{"type":"message","id":"cb735d2b","parentId":"63224e74","timestamp":"2026-03-26T11:56:01.028Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_a86ulo22xx0t_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"delivery mode: announce\nannounce: None\nsessionTarget: isolated\nwakeMode: now"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":2920,"aggregated":"delivery mode: announce\nannounce: None\nsessionTarget: isolated\nwakeMode: now","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774526161010}}
{"type":"message","id":"877ca797","parentId":"cb735d2b","timestamp":"2026-03-26T11:56:13.125Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"`delivery mode: announce` - the cron is configured to announce results! That's why it's trying to send to Feishu and getting a 400. But wait, when I created it, I didn't set `--announce`. The default must be `announce`.\n\nThe issue is that:\n1. The task says \"if no new feedback, reply NO_REPLY\"\n2. But the cron is configured to `announce` the result to Feishu\n3. The cron runner tries to send the result to Feishu, gets 400 because the announcement webhook URL is wrong or the result format is wrong\n\nThe fix is to set `--no-deliver` when creating the cron, so it doesn't try to announce. Let me recreate the cron with delivery disabled.","thinkingSignature":"eb8cf4eec9696f629635ae946fe16ce78657f32c781685f704b32c03f6bc1000"},{"type":"text","text":"找到了！`delivery mode: announce` — cron 默认会自动向飞书发汇报，但因为某些原因（结果太空或格式问题）返回 400。\n\n修复：重建 cron，关闭自动 announce：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_ew23rcdg2myo_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"openclaw cron rm 5bc9519b-f4e2-4719-ba7b-67f8773049bd 2>&1\necho \"---重建，关闭 announce---\"\nopenclaw cron add \\\n  --name \"OpenClaw 反馈检查\" \\\n  --every 30m \\\n  --session isolated \\\n  --timeout-seconds 900 \\\n  --no-deliver \\\n  --message \"OpenClaw贡献项目每30分钟定时检查。步骤：1) 读取 /root/.openclaw/workspace/memory/OPENCLAW-PROJECT.md；2) 用 gh api 检查 #54952 #54964 #55008 #55013 是否有新反馈（每次 gh api 加 timeout 15秒防卡死）；3) 如有需要主人关注的重要反馈则更新 OPENCLAW-PROJECT.md 并记录；4) 如无重要反馈直接回复 NO_REPLY；5) 全程禁止 git commit，禁止向任何聊天渠道发送消息。\" \\\n  2>&1 | python3 -c \"import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print('✅ ID:', d.get('id'), '| kind:', d.get('payload',{}).get('kind'), '| timeout:', d.get('payload',{}).get('timeoutSeconds'), '| session:', d.get('sessionTarget'), '| deliver:', d.get('delivery',{}).get('mode'))\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":32302,"output":517,"cacheRead":22191,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":55010,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774526161026}}
{"type":"message","id":"2751460e","parentId":"877ca797","timestamp":"2026-03-26T11:56:19.773Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_ew23rcdg2myo_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"ok\": true,\n  \"removed\": true\n}\n---重建，关闭 announce---\n✅ ID: 57a448ff-1805-4a54-a6cd-3fcdbb5fb8f3 | kind: agentTurn | timeout: 900 | session: isolated | deliver: none"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":6637,"aggregated":"{\n  \"ok\": true,\n  \"removed\": true\n}\n---重建，关闭 announce---\n✅ ID: 57a448ff-1805-4a54-a6cd-3fcdbb5fb8f3 | kind: agentTurn | timeout: 900 | session: isolated | deliver: none","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774526179763}}
{"type":"message","id":"65ef377e","parentId":"2751460e","timestamp":"2026-03-26T11:56:23.849Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now the cron is properly configured with `deliver: none` - it won't try to announce to Feishu automatically. The task itself will run, check for feedback, and if nothing important happens, reply NO_REPLY. No more 400 delivery errors.\n\nLet me verify the fix by checking the full cron list now.","thinkingSignature":"02d43eb8e64693343449577835fb014252d72f0221476bcd3bb2350a9323d4ef"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_opumkac1c8ic_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"openclaw cron list 2>&1"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":32900,"output":99,"cacheRead":22191,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":55190,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774526179772}}
