{"type":"message","id":"f7d29506","parentId":"d03eee58","timestamp":"2026-03-26T14:39:26.609Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I can see there are memory files. The key question is: does the cron job at midnight create a daily diary that would include the OpenClaw project status? And is the OPENCLAW-PROJECT.md being kept up to date?\n\nLooking at what we have:\n- `OPENCLAW-PROJECT.md` - updated throughout today with current project status\n- `memory-daily-create` cron at midnight should create a daily diary\n\nThe issue is: the daily cron that creates the diary might not specifically extract the OpenClaw project status. Let me check the cron message to see what it does.\n\nBut more importantly - the OPENCLAW-PROJECT.md is the single source of truth file and it's being kept updated. \n\nSo when the system restarts or picks up fresh tomorrow, as long as it reads OPENCLAW-PROJECT.md it'll have the context. The real vulnerability is that the cron task at midnight might create a diary entry but not capture the OpenClaw project state specifically. What's actually needed is a mechanism that preserves the OpenClaw project status in a persistent, retrievable format that survives restarts - which is what OPENCLAW-PROJECT.md already does, but I should verify the cron is actually writing to it at the end of today.\n\nThe user is right to be concerned though. Tomorrow morning when I start fresh, I need to be able to pick up exactly where we left off without having to re-read everything. The evening workspace wrap-up cron should handle this, but it keeps timing out, so I need to either fix that cron or create a standalone mechanism that captures the OpenClaw project state separately from the daily diary.","thinkingSignature":"a6a50c32aad28f59f56f55863acf9bcc967ad382621230dc827996f091c259af"},{"type":"text","text":"好问题，让我检查一下现有机制：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_d35x1d2s7wje_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cat /root/.open